{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Hyssop.</b> A species of herb that has stalks." "<b>A bundle of hyssop.</b> Three stalks are called a bundle (Shabbat 109)." "<b>That is in the basin.</b> In the vessel, as in ״סִפּוֹת כֶּסֶף״." "<b>Of the blood that is in the basin.</b> Why did he go back and repeat it? Lest you say one dipping suffices for all three applications — therefore it says again אֲשֶׁר בַּסַּף, so that each and every application of the blood that is in the basin requires its own dipping (Mekhilta)." "<b>And you shall not go out, etc.</b> This teaches that once permission was given to the Destroyer to strike, he does not distinguish between righteous and wicked (ibid.); and night is the domain of the destroyers, as it says ״בּוֹ תִּרְמֹס כָּל חַיְתוֹ יָעַר״ (Psalms 104)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:45.320819662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}